{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109100","id":2705484481,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6hQmrB","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109100","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109100.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109100.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109100","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109100/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109100/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109100/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/af8bdac5a9fadda049acc3f40cbcbc5f43fffe7d","number":109100,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix snapping logic in Range","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR is a fix for issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095. Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes Range's step feature to use `r128.h` instead of the existing algorithm.\r\n\r\nIn master:\r\n\r\n```\r\n0.1 -> 0.09999999999126885\r\n0.2 -> 0.19999999999708962\r\n0.3 -> 0.29999999998835847\r\n0.4 -> 0.39999999999417923\r\n0.5 -> 0.5\r\n0.6 -> 0.5999999999912689\r\n0.7 -> 0.6999999999970896\r\n0.8 -> 0.7999999999883585\r\n0.9 -> 0.8999999999941792\r\n1.0 -> 1.0\r\n1.1 -> 1.0999999999912689\r\n1.2 -> 1.1999999999970896\r\n1.3 -> 1.2999999999883585\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this PR: everything works as expected.\r\n\r\nOld PR description:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n\r\nThis PR is a partial fix for issue https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107095, but not a full fix.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes Range's step feature to use `Math::snapped` instead of this custom algorithm.\r\n\r\nWith this PR:\r\n\r\n```\r\n0.1 -> 0.09999999999999999\r\n0.2 -> 0.19999999999999998\r\n0.3 -> 0.3\r\n0.4 -> 0.39999999999999997\r\n0.5 -> 0.5\r\n0.6 -> 0.6\r\n0.7 -> 0.7\r\n0.8 -> 0.7999999999999999\r\n0.9 -> 0.8999999999999999\r\n1.0 -> 1.0\r\n1.1 -> 1.0999999999999999\r\n1.2 -> 1.2\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe new results with this PR are approximately 99.9995% closer to the desired value, and in some cases, match exactly.\r\n\r\nOk... but what about fixing this further? Unfortunately, it's not really possible to do that. The `step` value we're plugging into `Math::snapped` simply doesn't have enough precision for this. When a property hint has a step size of `0.001`, that gets converted into the nearest possible float, which is technically `0.00100000000000000002081668171172`. And, the number `0.1` is technically not a multiple of that value, even though it is a multiple of the decimal `0.001`.\r\n\r\nThe only solution I can think of to fix this further would be to use 128-bit floats instead of 64-bit floats, store the step size in 128-bit, do the math in 128-bit, and then store the computed value as 64-bit. If we were using C++23 or later, we could switch to [`std::float128_t`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/floating-point.html). Without C++23, the best we could do is platform-specific compiler extensions or a library. My recommendation is, for now, merge the 99.9995% fix in this PR while Godot uses C++17, and then we can switch the step size to 128-bit in the future when Godot requires C++23.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/pr